// expect-error: the code running beside the thread that started it
// BUG-1671: a join ends the thread it joins — not a thread THAT thread detached. `child` starts
// `grandchild` fire-and-forget and returns; main joins `child` and writes `g` while `grandchild` is still
// writing it. A thread was judged against the window of its OWN spawn site only; it runs inside every
// thread that can execute the function that spawns it, so it is judged against their windows too — and
// once a thread on the way down is detached, such a window no longer closes at a join.
// (race_free.v: `after t n u` says u has finished; it says nothing of what u started.)
u32 flagx;
u32 g;
void grandchild() { @atomic_store(&flagx, 1); for (u32 i = 0; i < 100000; i += 1) { g += 1; } }
void child() { spawn grandchild(); }
i32 main() {
    ThreadHandle t = spawn child();
    t.join();
    for (u32 i = 0; i < 100000; i += 1) { g += 1; }
    return 0;
}
